"skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le03ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le03ob11re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn5le03ob11re2img05.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn5le03ob11re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Hey Vanessa! Moved out and on your own now, eh? I'm excited to see your new place!  <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I'll take you on a tour of it! We'll start in the living room!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Wow, it looks bigger than I thought, not as small as I thought it'd be.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You won't believe all of the apartment listings I looked through. Will you come and visit me soon?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: It looks like I've got to. Your place looks awesome! I love that couch!<br>", "id": 1, "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn5le03ob11re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: There's lots of space! It's more spacious than the apartment I looked at a few blocks down.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Show me more.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Let me show you my bedroom and the ensuite. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: An ensuite? That's sweet! <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yes and guess what I got!<br>", "id": 2, "time": "23800"}, {"image": "engenn5le03ob11re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: What?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: My own washer and dryer! <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: That's incredible! Will you buy more furniture? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I'll buy a better refrigerator. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Will you cook more now?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I won't be doing that.<br>", "id": 3, "time": "37500"}]}}], "id": 1}], "type": "scholar", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Vanessa's Stories", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Brand New Place to Live", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe rooms, homes and objects in buildings in common social and work situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Describing a New Home", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you compare two things, you use a <span class=\"strong\">comparative</span>. You can use <span class=\"italic\">than</span> or  <span class=\"italic\">as \u2026 as. </span>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">We can show that two things are equal by using <span class=\"strong\">as + adjective + as</span></span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">There</span> is no difference between the two compared objects or ideas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">We can show that two things are not equal by using</span> <span class=\"strong\">not + as + adjective + as</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When comparing with<span class=\"italic\"> than, the adjective you use can change  depending on the number of syllables it has: <ul><li>1-syllable adjectives: add -er to the adjective<br><span class=\"italic\"> nice \u2192 nicer</span> </li><li> 2-syllable adjectives ending in -y: change the -y to -ier <br><span class=\"italic\">busy \u2192 busier </span> </li><li>Adjectives with 3 or more syllables: use more with the unchanged adjective<br> <span class=\"italic\">expensive \u2192 more expensive</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Certain adjectives have irregular forms in the comparative. For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">good \u2192 better<br>bad \u2192 worse</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "This couch is nicer than that couch.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "This street is busier than my old street.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My condo was more expensive than the other apartment.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking about Actions and Events", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you use the Future tense, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"italic\">will</span>. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Affirmative \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"will + base form of the verb (long form)  'll + base form of the verb (short form)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I will show you around my apartment. <br>I'll come visit you in the fall. </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Negative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"will not + base form of the verb (long form) won't + base form of the verb (short form)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You will not believe it!<br>I won't come in the winter.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Interrogative \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Will or Won't + subject + base form of the verb. (yes-no question)<br> Wh-word + will or won't + subject + base form of the verb (wh-question)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Will you buy some furniture?<br>Won't you cook dinner?</span> <br><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> What will you cook?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to move out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to go live in a different place", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I want to move out when I'm done school.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are the words to review. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "living room", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the main room in a house where people relax", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The living room has a large television. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "apartment listing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small advertisement for an apartment ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  You won't find any apartment listings there.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "spacious", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having a large amount of space", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Look at this spacious living room.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bedroom", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a room for sleeping in", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's a one-bedroom condo.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ensuite", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a bathroom that is joined to a bedroom", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The apartment unit includes an ensuite.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "washer and dryer", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a washing machine and a clothes dryer", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I have to buy a washer and dryer.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "furniture", "type": "name"}, {"content": "large objects you use in a home", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The apartment includes furniture.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob11aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "refrigerator", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large piece of kitchen equipment you use to  keep food cool", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The kitchen includes a refrigerator. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob11aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Look through magazines. Go on the Internet.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find pictures of different rooms you like.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find pictures of objects in rooms you like.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose two different rooms. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare them. Use comparatives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 4-5 sentences that describe each room.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your sentences aloud to your class.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about rooms and objects in them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use comparatives when talking about rooms.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my sentences aloud.", "type": "text"}]}]}